nking":"Perfect! I can see:\n1. The farmers_markets column in the farmers_markets table has state-level counts\n2. The census table has a \"United States\" row with POPESTIMATE2025 = 341,784,857\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Sum all farmers markets from the farmers_markets table\n2. Get the U.S. population from census (341,784,857)\n3. Calculate: (total farmers markets / population) * 100,000\n\nNow I need to create a build script that will join these two datasets and create a metric. According to the skill, I should create one build script that reads both sources and joins them.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create a derived metric by joining both sources and calculating farmers markets per 100,000 residents:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01BVuKMEwSzq2oqqcgzamVyK","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/fm_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Sum all farmers markets and get US population\nfm_total = fact.aggregate(total_fm=fact.farmers_markets.sum())\nus_pop = ref.filter(ref.NAME == 'United States').select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n\n# Join on constant key and calculate per capita metric\nfm_total_with_key = fm_total.mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\nus_pop_with_key = us_pop.mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\nexpr = (\n    fm_total_with_key.join(us_pop_with_key, fm_total_with_key.k == us_pop_with_key.k)\n    .mutate(fm_per_100k=fm_total_with_key.total_fm / us_pop_with_key.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n    .select(\"total_fm\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"fm_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":753,"cacheRead":18655,"cacheWrite":1721,"totalTokens":21143,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.003765,"cacheRead":0.0018655000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.00215125,"total":0.007795750000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":152},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915175631,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78FY9NyNASKCgkmnGpf","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01BVuKMEwSzq2oqqcgzamVyK","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1251 bytes to .xorq/scripts/fm_per_capita.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915184125},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me build this script:","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01TyVek9jNB7DhQ5yPQRNbB1","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"xorq build .xorq/scripts/fm_per_capita.py --builds-dir .xorq/builds --emit-build-path-to /tmp/metric_bp.txt && cat /tmp/metric_bp.txt"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":120,"cacheRead":20376,"cacheWrite":795,"totalTokens":21304,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0006000000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0020376,"cacheWrite":0.00099375,"total":0.00364435},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":12},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915184126,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78G8mEQrZXZ4zhLHGs1","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01TyVek9jNB7DhQ5yPQRNbB1","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Building expr from .xorq/scripts/fm_per_capita.py\n/nix/store/yvlv6n4rx6dnnvhi7sgc5lm0152pa8mx-pi-xorq-duel-dev-env/lib/python3.13/site-packages/xorq/ibis_yaml/sql.py:120: UserWarning: <xorq.backends.pandas.Backend 